<< /A 63 0 R /Alt (Bar chart illustrating DASS21 factor loadings across three timepoints, labeled T0, T1, and T2, with standardized loading values on the Y-axis and individual items on the X-axis. Each timepoint is represented by a different color, showing variability in standardized loadings across items and timepoints.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 64 0 R /Alt (Heatmap titled \215CDRISC25: Tucker\220s Congruence\216 shows pairwise congruence between timepoints T0, T1, and T2, with values ranging from 0.958 to 1.000. Color bar ranges from 0.800 to 1.000.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 65 0 R /Alt (Network diagram showing interconnected psychological variables such as Agreeableness, Depression, Resilience, Anxiety, Leadership, and others, color-coded by categories like Personality, Distress, and Resilience. Solid green lines indicate positive relationships, dashed red lines indicate negative relationships, and line thickness suggests relationship strength. A legend specifies category and edge meanings.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 66 0 R /Alt (Bar chart graphic comparing centrality indices for multiple variables in a cross-sectional network, grouped into Strength, Betweenness, and Closeness panels. Depression T zero and OCB Altruism score highest in Strength, OCB Sportsmanship leads Betweenness, and Resilience T zero leads Closeness. Each panel ranks variables by their respective centrality measure.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 67 0 R /Alt (Heatmap visualization depicting edge inclusion proportions for various psychological and behavioral variables as part of a cross-sectional network analysis using bootstrap. Color gradient from yellow to dark red indicates lower to higher inclusion proportions, with a reference scale bar labeled \215Inclusion Proportion\216 ranging from zero to one.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 45 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 68 0 R /Alt (Network diagram titled \215Temporal Psychological Network: DASS and Resilience \(T0, T1, T2\)\216 showing interconnected colored nodes representing depression \(red\), anxiety \(orange\), stress \(yellow\), and resilience \(green\) at three time points. Green solid lines indicate positive relationships, while red dashed lines indicate negative relationships. Legend explains node colors and edge meanings.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 46 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 69 0 R /Alt (Bar chart graphic with three panels displaying centrality indices for a temporal network: Strength, Betweenness, and Closeness. Each panel shows color-coded horizontal bars for different variables across multiple time points, comparing their centrality values.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 47 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 70 0 R /Alt (Four-panel figure for latent profile analysis model selection. Top left line chart shows BIC decreasing as the number of profiles rises from two to five. Top right line chart shows AIC also decreasing across the same range. Bottom left line chart shows entropy increasing and peaking at four profiles, then slightly declining at five. Bottom right line chart shows silhouette values decreasing as the number of profiles increases.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 47 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 71 0 R /Alt (Radar chart comparing five latent profiles using standardized means for factors including Openness, Conscientiousness, Extraversion, Agreeableness, Neuroticism, Depression T0, Anxiety T0, Stress T0, Resilience T0, and Leadership. Each profile is distinguished by a different color and plotted with connected data points and shaded areas. A legend in the top right indicates which color corresponds to each profile number.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 48 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
26 0 obj
<< /A 72 0 R /Alt (Bar chart titled \215Latent Profile Means\216 comparing standardized means for five profiles across ten personality and psychological traits, with each profile represented by different colored bars as shown in the legend.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 48 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
27 0 obj
<< /A 73 0 R /Alt (Five vertically stacked data visualizations illustrate latent profile analysis results: boxplots showing outcome variables across five profiles, four line charts comparing model selection criteria by profile number, a radar chart depicting standardized means for profile characterization across traits, and a heatmap showing profile concordance between sensitivity and primary analyses with count values.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 49 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
28 0 obj
<< /A 74 0 R /Alt (Bar chart illustrates factors affecting academic performance using nomogram points, with odds ratios shown. Gender has the strongest positive association, while dass_depression_t0 and bfi_openness have negative associations. Green bars denote positive risk, red bars negative.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 50 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
29 0 obj
<< /A 75 0 R /Alt (Forest plot graphic depicting odds ratios and ninety-five percent confidence intervals for academic performance by predictor variable, with gender showing the highest odds ratio and widest confidence interval, and a red vertical reference line at one.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 50 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
30 0 obj
<< /A 76 0 R /Alt (Line graph calibration plot comparing model-predicted probabilities versus observed proportions for academic performance, with a dashed diagonal line for perfect calibration and a legend showing AUC 0.682 and Brier score 0.232.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 51 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
